{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And now the word, etc.</b> HaShem revealed this sod, for three years remained. And the meaning is like a hired laborer, every day he looks forward in his soul to when the end will arrive — so the prophet rejoiced at the appointed time of their doom." "<b>And it shall be slight.</b> His glory, which is a great multitude, and but a tiny remnant shall remain." "<b>Not great.</b> Not a great people in number — as is known כבירים (Job 34:24) — or its meaning is: no great man shall remain of them, like הן אל כביר (ibid. 36:5)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "Bracketed editorial note [צ\"ל וטעם] indicates a correction from והטעם to וטעם; translated according to corrected reading."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:05.934241944Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}